      "start": 0.76,
      "end": 2.26,
      "text": "Hi, how are you holding up?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 9.42,
      "end": 16.69,
      "text": "The basics are water, snacks, a light rain jacket, sunscreen and a charged phone. A small first aid kit is a good idea too."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 21.62,
      "end": 27.62,
      "text": "About half a litre per hour of hiking, more if it's hot. For a four hour walk, two litres is a safe amount."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 35.15,
      "end": 39.88,
      "text": "Only if you know there's safe water along the way. Streams aren't safe to drink without a filter."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 44.93,
      "end": 53.17,
      "text": "Things that are easy to eat on the move, like nuts, dried fruit, cereal bars or a sandwich. Salty snacks are nice if you sweat a lot."
